### Issue description

### Description
When using Jade’s EntityLootTableProvider.Client.appendTooltip, the game can crash due to invalid argument types being passed into Component.translatable. Specifically, a ResourceLocation / Identifier is passed directly, which is not a supported argument type.

This results in a client crash during tooltip/narration rendering.

## Crash Cause

Minecraft only allows the following argument types in Component.translatable:

Component
String
Number
Boolean

However, A Identifier is being passed directly (e.g. minecraft:entities/*), which triggers an IllegalArgumentException.

## Expected Behavior
Tooltip rendering should not crash even if unsupported argument types are passed. All arguments should be safely converted before being passed into Component.translatable.

## Suggested Upstream Fix

In EntityLootTableProvider.Client.appendTooltip, sanitize all arguments before passing them to Component.translatable:

Convert Identifier → String
Ensure all varargs are valid Minecraft chat component types
Fallback: String.valueOf(arg) for unknown types

## Temporary Fix (Mixin Workaround)
A Mixin is used to sanitize arguments before they reach Component.translatable.
```java
@Mixin(EntityLootTableProvider.Client.class)
public class JadeLootTableFixMixin {

    @ModifyArg(
        method = "appendTooltip",
        at = @At(
            value = "INVOKE",
            target = "Lnet/minecraft/network/chat/Component;translatable(Ljava/lang/String;[Ljava/lang/Object;)Lnet/minecraft/network/chat/MutableComponent;"
        ),
        index = 1
    )
    private Object[] fixLootTableNarrationArgs(Object[] originalArgs) {
        Object[] fixed = new Object[originalArgs.length];

        for (int i = 0; i < originalArgs.length; i++) {
            Object arg = originalArgs[i];

            if (arg instanceof Identifier rl) {
                fixed[i] = rl.toString();
            } else if (
                !(arg instanceof Component) &&
                !(arg instanceof String) &&
                !(arg instanceof Number) &&
                !(arg instanceof Boolean)
            ) {
                fixed[i] = String.valueOf(arg);
            } else {
                fixed[i] = arg;
            }
        }

        return fixed;
    }
}
```

## Steps to Reproduce
- Launch Minecraft with Jade installed (NeoForge environment)
- Enter a world (singleplayer or multiplayer)
- Turn on loot table in the debug section config for jade
- Spawn or locate any mob (e.g., a vanilla entity or modded entity such as creaking, etc)
- Look at the mob to trigger Jade’s entity tooltip overlay
- Observe crash when Jade attempts to display loot table debug information

